Every clinician should consider a cumulative-nonopioid-medication-dosage during an opioid-therapy.
A cumulative-nonopioid-medication-dosage-example is a cumulative-acetaminophen-dosage-example.
If a patient takes a combined-nonopioid-medication with an opioid and the combined-nonopioid-medication has a decreased-clearance in the patient then every clinician should consider a toxic-medication-accumulation for the combined-nonopioid-medication during an opioid-therapy for the patient.
If a combined-nonopioid-medication has a decreased-clearance then it is possible that the decreased-clearance causes a toxic-medication-accumulation for the combined-nonopioid-medication.
